# Punch (Assignment 2b)

A bash-lite command language, implemented as a tree-walking interpreter in C++17 (Unix).

## Build and run
    make                      # or: g++ -std=c++17 -Wall src/*.cpp -o punch
    ./punch script.punch      # run a script
    ./punch --tokens f.punch  # print the token stream (lexer output)
    ./punch --ast f.punch     # print the syntax tree (from step 42)
    make test                 # run tests/run_tests.sh

## Pipeline
    source -> Lexer -> tokens -> Parser -> AST -> Analyser -> Interpreter

